      "body": "prisma.room.delete({ where: { slug, adminId } }) passes adminId in the where of a singular delete. Prisma requires the where argument of delete/findUnique/update to match a unique criterion, and adminId is not unique (slug is). This throws a PrismaClientValidationError at runtime, which is not PrismaClientKnownRequestError/P2025, so the catch block does not handle it: legitimate deletes by the admin fail with 500 instead of 204, and the intended 404 for rooms owned by others is never returned.\n\nSuggested fix (model-generated, not tested):\n```suggestion\n    prisma.room.deleteMany({\n      where: { slug, adminId },\n    });\n```",
